"evidence":["Plan ships both a macOS `sandbox-exec` snippet and a Linux `bwrap` invocation, each verified only as literal presence ('the `(deny file-write*)` and `sandbox-exec -f` literals are present', '`--ro-bind / /`, `--dev`, `--proc` ...')","The selection/ordering ('Neither mechanism present, or `bwrap` present but unable to namespace: ...') appears only in prose, and no AC asserts the skill states the try-macOS / try-Linux-with-probe / else-fallback ORDER as a single co-located decision rule","T8(b): a processing/decision rule referenced but not co-located with the schema (here, the invocation set) that needs it"],"finding":"The skill ships two platform-specific sandbox invocations plus a capability probe and a fallback, but the acceptance criteria verify each fragment's presence independently and never require the ordered SELECTION/decision rule that tells the agent which mechanism to attempt on which platform and how probe-failure sequences into the fallback. The decision rule lives only in the 'When no sandbox is available' prose and is not co-located with the invocations as a verified protocol.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3021ccfb7cae3837","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (macOS/Linux/probe/fallback bullets) vs. 'When no sandbox is available' section","norm_id":"n5b45ff39c03677dc","priority":0.4813,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An agent on Linux reads the macOS snippet first, or runs bwrap without the capability probe because the ordering was never stated as a rule the agent must follow","The regression test passes because all fragments are present, yet the skill lacks a single ordered decision rule linking probe-failure to the fallback"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'Each skill presents the three mechanisms as one ordered decision rule (macOS sandbox-exec -> Linux bwrap gated on the capability probe -> injected-seam fallback), co-located with the invocations; verified by the test asserting the ordering language and probe-before-bwrap sequencing.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: better","verify command `grep -rilE \"sandbox-exec|bwrap|bubblewrap\" examples/agent-skills/` inspects output with `grep` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is