time","An operator following the inline snippet gets weaker isolation (no HOME isolation, venv writable) than the CI gate that shares the same threat model"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Update the rationale to acknowledge mutation_sandbox.py has landed, and state the positive reason for still inlining (skill text must be self-contained and shell-runnable with no repo dependency) — or pivot the skill guidance to call `python scripts/mutation_sandbox.py -- <cmd>` and drop the duplicated snippets.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State explicitly that the sandbox permits destruction WITHIN the worktree (an accepted residual because the worktree is a recoverable git checkout), and consider matching the e668 wrapper by setting HOME to a non-existent path in the inline snippets so home-adjacent writes fail loudly.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["macOS snippet: '(allow file-write* (subpath \"$PWD\") (subpath \"$SBX\") ...)'","Linux snippet: 'bwrap --ro-bind / / ... --bind \"$PWD\" \"$PWD\"'","e668 hardens beyond this with HOME set to a non-existent path; the inline snippet has no HOME handling","Incident cause per e668: 'a test exec'd that script with an empty path variable, and the glob expanded to rm -rf /*' — an empty/relative variant could resolve within $PWD"],"finding":"The macOS profile allow-lists writes to `(subpath \"$PWD\")` and the Linux invocation does `--bind \"$PWD\" \"$PWD\"`, and neither isolates HOME. A defect-seeded mutation of deletion code runs inside $PWD, so a mutated deletion whose target resolves within the worktree (or an empty path variable expanding relative to cwd, the incident's shape) can still destroy the worktree — including the agent's uncommitted fix and code-under-test — while the plan asserts only that writes OUTSIDE the worktree are denied and does not name this residual blast radius.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f407d03b29042a70d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'The invocations, in full' and AC line 1","norm_id":"na680da439a3f58a7","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A mutation reverts a guard so a deletion path resolves to a relative or worktree-internal directory that is fully writable under the profile","Home-directory-adjacent writes the e668 wrapper catches with a nonexistent HOME are silently permitted here"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the mechanism section noting the worktree remains writable-by-design (recoverable via git) and add `HOME=/nonexistent` (or an env override) to both the sandbox-exec and bwrap invocations to match the sibling ticket's home-isolation guarantee.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Note in the skill text that `sandbox-exec` is deprecated-but-functional on current macOS, so operators understand the durability caveat and the fallback (injected-seam) path when it is eventually removed.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'Verified on macOS 26.5.2: a write outside $SBX was denied' — no mention that sandbox-exec is deprecated.","Retrieved (dev.to/hassekf): 'The macOS 26.5.2 man page for sandbox-exec marks it deprecated, and it works today anyway.'","Retrieved (Stack Overflow 56703697): 'in the newest MacOS the sandbox-exec command is DEPRECATED.'","Retrieved (OpenAI Codex discussion #5523): 'Even though sandbox-exec is deprecated, it still works as a temporary layer of protection.'"],"finding":"The macOS invocation relies on `sandbox-exec`, which is marked DEPRECATED on current macOS (including 26.5.2, the version the plan says it verified on); the plan cites the verification but not the deprecation, leaving a durability/prior-art risk unacknowledged.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f39af358a03f4b11c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"\"The invocations, in full\" — macOS snippet / AC 'complete, self-contained macOS snippet'","norm_id":"n1c2280b27ab9df74","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future macOS removes or further restricts sandbox-exec and the skill's inline command silently stops sandboxing while agents keep running mutations."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the `(allow default)`/deny-file-write* posture against the stronger deny-by-default allow-list alternative for the hostile-code threat model, or scope the claim to filesystem-deletion protection only (which is the incident it addresses).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan profile: '(allow default) (deny file-write*) (allow file-write* (subpath \"$PWD\") ...)'","Plan framing: 'a seeded defect is arbitrary code, so the run executes hostile code'.","Retrieved (Pillar Security, 'Week of Sandbox Escapes Day 1'): 'Antigravity went with (allow default). That single line at the top of the profile converts it to a denylist' — the subject of a documented escape write-up covering Antigravity/Codex/Cursor allow-default profiles."],"finding":"The macOS profile uses the `(allow default)` denylist posture, which retrieved security prior art documents as the weaker sandbox model with known escapes; the plan does not weigh a deny-by-default (allow-list) profile, even though its own threat model is hostile arbitrary code.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59a667259552a987","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"\"The invocations, in full\" — macOS `p.sb` heredoc (`(allow default)` / `(deny file-write*)`)","norm_id":"na6b9462622be9ee1","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Hostile mutation code exploits a non-file-write vector (e.g. process, network, pre-opened fd) that `(allow default)` leaves permitted, since the plan only denies file-write*."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence scoping the macOS profile: it protects against filesystem writes/deletion (the 2026-08-26 vector) and is not a general-purpose hostile-code jail; a deny-by-default allow-list would be stronger but broader than this rule requires.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood